            {
                "entry_id": "fe2970de-be25-334f-abc1-8b0ae924cf5a",
                "word": "boniment",
                "pos": "noun",
                "lang_code": "fr",
                "forms": [
                    {
                        "form_id": "d558d2d4-2a31-44fa-b7c8-73f34b1ff6a2",
                        "entry_id": "fe2970de-be25-334f-abc1-8b0ae924cf5a",
                        "tags": [
                            "plural"
                        ],
                        "form": "boniments"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "5ac16da0-6b9a-3b74-99a9-30fff09799ae",
                        "entry_id": "fe2970de-be25-334f-abc1-8b0ae924cf5a",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Propos que débitent les camelots, les charlatans et les saltimbanques pour attirer les clients."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "e99e35b6-a1c9-4493-9c66-bf1d7cf7a55a",
                                "sense_id": "5ac16da0-6b9a-3b74-99a9-30fff09799ae",
                                "text": "Faire un boniment, Débiter un boniment, vanter sa marchandise."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "7858b78e-4a91-4b3c-950d-c36065455601",
                                "sense_id": "5ac16da0-6b9a-3b74-99a9-30fff09799ae",
                                "text": "— Tu crois ça, toi ? Eh bien, moi je dis qu’il faut que les curés nous prennent sérieusement pour des poires, de nous envoyer des boniments comme ça !"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "77befa04-816b-478d-836a-62fac390c471",
                                "sense_id": "5ac16da0-6b9a-3b74-99a9-30fff09799ae",
                                "text": "Les boniments des camelots. Quand un sergent de ville s’éloigne, un camelot surgit. Coiffés d’une casquette, le visage animé, la moustache déteinte, ils parlent avec chaleur, car leurs passions sont violentes et ils veulent gagner de quoi manger et de quoi boire."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "5d9bd701-47a9-41f0-8389-72cdb5d06e0b",
                                "sense_id": "5ac16da0-6b9a-3b74-99a9-30fff09799ae",
                                "text": "Ton frère est venu me voir sur la fin de l’après-midi. Il m’a redit tous les boniments du curé, un peu plus raides tout de même."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "bb3fffba-a067-4804-b3e8-4a0fd431f288",
                                "sense_id": "5ac16da0-6b9a-3b74-99a9-30fff09799ae",
                                "text": "Puis, faisant tourner alternativement chacune des roues comme un camelot qui veut montrer le bon fonctionnement d’un article, il poursuit son boniment d’un ton convaincu."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "d1ce1cbc-c85b-374b-aacf-3bab1c140fb4",
                        "entry_id": "fe2970de-be25-334f-abc1-8b0ae924cf5a",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Par extension, synonyme de mensonge hypocrite ou maniéré ; tartuferie, baratin, bobard, racontar."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": []
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "aeba2610-682b-41bc-9a2e-19ba05595256",
                        "source_entry_id": "fe2970de-be25-334f-abc1-8b0ae924cf5a",
                        "target_lang_word": "Lügengeschichte",
                        "target_lang_code": "de",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "Lügengeschichte",
                                "target_lang_code": "de",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "de8a3a4e-32d9-39c7-b2d1-c03aeda77cb2",
                                        "entry_id": "db33d4b3-f10a-3b97-a71f-e2f4c81961cf",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "unwahre, erlogene Geschichte"
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "6a3a5be2-8493-4542-a914-c21a5202267c",
                                                "sense_id": "de8a3a4e-32d9-39c7-b2d1-c03aeda77cb2",
                                                "text": "Die bekanntesten Lügengeschichten stammen von Baron Münchhausen."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "b1142fd9-940a-4e70-953d-999db5b0977c",
                                                "sense_id": "de8a3a4e-32d9-39c7-b2d1-c03aeda77cb2",
                                                "text": "„In der Lügengeschichte gibt es nicht nur einen inhaltlichen Konflikt zwischen Wirklichkeit und Lüge, der komisch wirkt, sondern es geht auch um einen Überlegenheitskonflikt zwischen Erzähler und Zuhörer.“"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "47829826-c5b1-461b-8e30-3bca279f6a82",
                                                "sense_id": "de8a3a4e-32d9-39c7-b2d1-c03aeda77cb2",
                                                "text": "„Murray erzählte mir eine Menge Lügengeschichten, die man über mein Verschwinden in Umlauf gesetzt hatte, und fragte mich unter anderem, ob ich einen kleinen Roman vom Abbate Chiari kenne, der gegen Ende des Karnevals erschienen sei.“"
                                            }
                                        ],
                                        "sense_index_json": "\"1\""
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "05e26ef9-7221-4237-a7c0-af0543c696e6",
                        "source_entry_id": "fe2970de-be25-334f-abc1-8b0ae924cf5a",
                        "target_lang_word": "spiel",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "spiel",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "ee0b2dcb-b2b3-326f-a372-2d1860b9c2c1",
                                        "entry_id": "d1355335-f00d-3b0f-8b78-c3ff655fcb2b",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A lengthy and extravagant speech or argument usually intended to persuade."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "b70d1456-baa5-4931-bc84-1207d7137838",
                                                "sense_id": "ee0b2dcb-b2b3-326f-a372-2d1860b9c2c1",
                                                "text": "I'd love to be there with a real pretty spiel / But three little words can explain how I feel"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "df4a8fc9-7eb5-4717-9de6-f7c66480d368",
                                                "sense_id": "ee0b2dcb-b2b3-326f-a372-2d1860b9c2c1",
                                                "text": "The spiel ran on; the sale was brief and brisk; / The bargains fell to bidders, one by one. / Hope flushed my cheekbones with a scarlet disk."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "a51688a8-2aed-4ab3-bab1-b8b634f93aaf",
                                                "sense_id": "ee0b2dcb-b2b3-326f-a372-2d1860b9c2c1",
                                                "text": "An Air Force recruiter (Gino Anania) visits her school and delivers a spiel about anti-terrorist successes in Iraq; she contradicts him with the plain facts of the 2001 attacks."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "e753b824-df25-3bf0-806f-e26ed20b0d5a",
                                        "entry_id": "d1355335-f00d-3b0f-8b78-c3ff655fcb2b",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "An early form of rap music."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "5df7ddc5-1220-458c-a170-c69e8372b849",
                                                "sense_id": "e753b824-df25-3bf0-806f-e26ed20b0d5a",
                                                "text": "Watt gets his turn on the mic too, delivering an amusingly disjointed rap (following Minutemen tradition, he calls it a spiel) on \"Me & You, Remembering.\""
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "d368c86e-5495-4f60-b75d-ce5290237011",
                                                "sense_id": "e753b824-df25-3bf0-806f-e26ed20b0d5a",
                                                "text": "A typical Last Poets song consisted of a \"spiel,\" an early form of rap where song verses were spoken over conga drum percussions or jazz music."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "ea0837f8-3c4e-4ca8-a509-0673d35af00c",
                                                "sense_id": "e753b824-df25-3bf0-806f-e26ed20b0d5a",
                                                "text": "Drawing on the smooth and steady rap style of disco DJs, the proto-rap spiel of the Last Poets and Gil Scott-Heron, various other American and African American oral traditions (including, as mentioned above, radio disc jockey practice) […]"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
                            {
                                "target_word": "spiel",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "cf0b4860-95dc-38ab-9f29-76575de5bc2c",
                                        "entry_id": "faa1eb3d-4995-3a27-bcab-50d824b7135a",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To talk at length."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "intransitive"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "deaf0ed6-4961-418a-9f13-37c136e9b8f4",
                                                "sense_id": "cf0b4860-95dc-38ab-9f29-76575de5bc2c",
                                                "text": "For a second our eyes met and he gave me a contemptuous smile, then he spieled again."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "2777d244-0a66-4d8b-8b70-813c0b02a4dd",
                                                "sense_id": "cf0b4860-95dc-38ab-9f29-76575de5bc2c",
                                                "text": "[…] Oedipa spotted among searchlights and staring crowds a KCUF mobile unit, with her husband Mucho inside it, spieling into a microphone."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "a87c5eb2-e962-36a9-8664-b568701766fa",
                                        "entry_id": "faa1eb3d-4995-3a27-bcab-50d824b7135a",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To give a sales pitch; to promote by speaking."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "intransitive"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": []
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
                            {
                                "target_word": "spiel",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "e2b3d9dc-7538-3f83-9803-b5d128145cd5",
                                        "entry_id": "25815e97-00fe-3776-823d-3b5a0fadf25a",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A game of curling."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "23dfa135-d3ea-4a61-a283-6f1f407ffb73",
                                                "sense_id": "e2b3d9dc-7538-3f83-9803-b5d128145cd5",
                                                "text": "The portion of ice set apart for a curling spiel was called the lead, rank, or rink (by which last name it is still described), and as it was then shorter than it is now — its ordinary length being 30 yards"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "01b69134-3d96-4595-813d-fe9ead635ec5",
                                                "sense_id": "e2b3d9dc-7538-3f83-9803-b5d128145cd5",
                                                "text": "On the Dock and Greensands the classical discus, or quoit, has in season due its modicum of disciples, (b) When the Nith is frozen over its surface becomes the scene of many a curling spiel"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "9923f49e-652b-4a94-9a84-216c3b2428f7",
                                                "sense_id": "e2b3d9dc-7538-3f83-9803-b5d128145cd5",
                                                "text": "A few organizational difficulties marred this spiel and the next, but thereafter most of the wrinkles were ironed out."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "561f94b9-89ed-4786-8d20-d90d35a2aa9a",
                        "source_entry_id": "fe2970de-be25-334f-abc1-8b0ae924cf5a",
                        "target_lang_word": "patter",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "patter",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "34a25d28-90b5-3cec-bfff-08d9fdba9598",
                                        "entry_id": "830ecaec-548a-39f8-b8dd-4d46232f8b3e",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A soft repeated sound, as of rain falling, or feet walking on a hard surface."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "8d73cb6f-d175-4f7a-badc-0e95407db98a",
                                                "sense_id": "34a25d28-90b5-3cec-bfff-08d9fdba9598",
                                                "text": "I could hear the patter of mice running about in the dark."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "d80ec1ec-2f78-4ae7-a7c2-6d12e9124af7",
                                                "sense_id": "34a25d28-90b5-3cec-bfff-08d9fdba9598",
                                                "text": "The patter of feet, and clatter of strap and swivel, seemed to swell into a bewildering din, but they were almost upon the fielato offices, where the carretera entered the town, before a rifle flashed."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
                            {
                                "target_word": "patter",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "2e672109-ef8a-38fc-97e1-70721b94f71a",
                                        "entry_id": "c79a7391-544d-3b37-abea-e041fc0d450a",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To make irregularly repeated sounds of low-to-moderate magnitude and lower-than-average pitch."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "cce0f022-3cd9-4278-a31d-4a8898a05361",
                                                "sense_id": "2e672109-ef8a-38fc-97e1-70721b94f71a",
                                                "text": "The bullets pattered into the log-cabin walls."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "fc3fb855-b318-4e43-90c4-8ba497eed152",
                                                "sense_id": "2e672109-ef8a-38fc-97e1-70721b94f71a",
                                                "text": "The stealing shower […] 'Tis scarce to patter heard."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "8d61f008-4e8b-3a3c-aa20-0ef679abaaf4",
                                        "entry_id": "c79a7391-544d-3b37-abea-e041fc0d450a",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To spatter; to sprinkle."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "d7815a9e-411a-4305-81ea-4dd3da827a4e",
                                                "sense_id": "8d61f008-4e8b-3a3c-aa20-0ef679abaaf4",
                                                "text": "1819 (published in 1835) Joseph Rodman Drake, The Culprit Fay\nPatter the water about the boat."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
                            {
                                "target_word": "patter",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "c7408ecd-f79c-3f30-9145-844ab7b6b1dc",
                                        "entry_id": "f803610d-b907-3823-97c8-4fac78a9b876",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Glib and rapid speech, such as from an auctioneer or a sports commentator."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "593f6a76-1fe9-4948-b638-83d8b1ab7607",
                                                "sense_id": "c7408ecd-f79c-3f30-9145-844ab7b6b1dc",
                                                "text": "This particularly rapid, unintelligible patter isn't generally heard, and if it is it doesn't matter."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "a2edb0ba-69eb-4c00-97a5-3010082f4c8f",
                                                "sense_id": "c7408ecd-f79c-3f30-9145-844ab7b6b1dc",
                                                "text": "Dad, I want to be a jock. All a jock needs is some hep patter and a real gone image. Now, they just don't teach that jazz in college."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "0f6fd6aa-6a65-4ef0-9483-bed9d1238aa8",
                                                "sense_id": "c7408ecd-f79c-3f30-9145-844ab7b6b1dc",
                                                "text": "“Did you say the bodies are getting mixed together with the toxic waste?” [sigh] “Now I got to look at the brochure. Yeah, that's what it says.” “By the way, you're really gonna have to work on your patter a little bit.”"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "ab349124-dc73-43c1-b72d-a09615ad4668",
                                                "sense_id": "c7408ecd-f79c-3f30-9145-844ab7b6b1dc",
                                                "text": "As a young man he [Beppe Grillo] performed with a guitar in local bars, but fans preferred his pre-show patter, and he evolved into a successful stand-up comedian."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
                            {
                                "target_word": "patter",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "1c0e2ba9-7111-3df6-abab-c362b394b8cd",
                                        "entry_id": "cf1e44a9-90d9-32ab-a889-525ec659a245",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To speak glibly and rapidly, as does an auctioneer or a sports commentator."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "4cf00104-1c6c-407e-831a-2a91de1d5a2f",
                                                "sense_id": "1c0e2ba9-7111-3df6-abab-c362b394b8cd",
                                                "text": "He showed a little of the pride of art in describing the management of his business, but he would not hear that he “pattered:” he talked to his customers, he declared, as any draper, who knew his business well, might talk to his."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
